{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2198-02-08 11:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you during this hospital stay. Can you tell me what brought you in today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2198-02-08 11:35:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, Doctor. I woke up this morning at 6 with really bad nausea and started vomiting. It’s been happening all day. I just got out of the hospital a few days ago for the same thing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2198-02-08 11:36:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And how have you been feeling since your last discharge?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2198-02-08 11:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I was doing okay. I was eating a little, taking my Reglan, Protonix, Zofran, and lisinopril like I was told. I thought I was past this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2198-02-08 11:38:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. The vomiting—has it been bloody or dark like coffee grounds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2198-02-08 11:38:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, it’s been greenish—bilious, I think. No blood. I did pass gas and had a bowel movement this morning, which is good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2198-02-08 11:39:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s reassuring. Any fevers, chest pain, or shortness of breath?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2198-02-08 11:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, nothing like that. Just the nausea and vomiting. I feel weak and kind of foggy from the Ativan they gave me in the ER."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2198-02-08 11:41:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. Your blood pressure was high when you came in—168 over 87—and your heart rate was fast. We’ll keep an eye on that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2198-02-08 11:42:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, it usually goes up when I’m stressed or vomiting a lot. Is that still a concern?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2198-02-08 11:43:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re managing it. You got IV metoprolol in the ER, and we’ll restart your lisinopril once you can keep things down. For now, we’re keeping you NPO—nothing by mouth."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2198-02-08 11:44:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I understand. What about my insulin? I’m worried about my sugars."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2198-02-08 11:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good question. We’re giving you IV fluids with some insulin to manage your blood sugar. Your glucose was 274 when you arrived. We’ll switch back to your usual insulin regimen as you start eating again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2198-02-08 11:46:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I’ve been trying so hard to stay on track."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2198-02-08 14:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi again. I wanted to update you on your labs. Your white count was high this morning—13.2—but it’s already coming down. We checked blood cultures to rule out infection, and they came back negative."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2198-02-08 14:21:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So no infection? That’s good, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2198-02-08 14:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, that’s good. Your chest X-ray was clear too—no pneumonia or other issues. We think this is another flare of your gastroparesis, especially since it feels just like your last episodes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2198-02-08 14:23:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "But I’ve been taking my meds. Why is this happening again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2198-02-08 14:24:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Sometimes even with good medication adherence, gastroparesis can flare. Your gastric pacer was adjusted just a week ago—could be part of the reason your stomach is still unstable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2198-02-08 14:25:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, right. I forgot about that. So what now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2198-02-08 14:26:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep giving you IV fluids and anti-nausea meds—Zofran, Compazine, and Ativan as needed. We’re also continuing your Protonix and Reglan through IV for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2198-02-09 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs are improving. Your white count is down to 6.6, and your sodium is a bit low—130—but stable. We’re watching it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2198-02-09 09:16:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is low sodium serious? I had that last time too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2198-02-09 09:17:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It can be, but yours isn’t causing symptoms. It’s likely due to vomiting and fluid shifts. We’re not giving extra sodium, but we’ll monitor it. Your TSH and cortisol were normal, so it’s not a hormone issue."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2198-02-09 09:18:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that’s a relief. Can I try sipping water yet?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2198-02-09 09:19:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re going to start with 5 mL sips of clear liquids every 15 minutes. If you keep that down for a few hours, we’ll advance to toast and tea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2198-02-09 09:20:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. I’m so ready to eat something."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2198-02-09 16:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi. Just checking in. The nurse said you’ve kept down small sips and had a bit of toast. How’s your nausea?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2198-02-09 16:31:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Much better. Still a little queasy, but not vomiting. I even took my Reglan pill without throwing it up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2198-02-09 16:32:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s excellent progress. We’ll keep advancing your diet slowly—BRAT diet for now: bananas, rice, applesauce, toast. Low fat, low fiber."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2198-02-09 16:33:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. What about my insulin? I took my long-acting at bedtime, but I’m not eating my usual meals."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2198-02-09 16:34:50",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re keeping your glargine at bedtime. For your lispro, we’re using a sliding scale based on your blood sugar since you’re not on regular meals yet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2198-02-10 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your urine culture came back. It showed mixed bacteria, but that’s likely contamination from skin or genital flora—nothing to treat."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2198-02-10 10:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So no UTI?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2198-02-10 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, no infection. Your electrolytes are stable, and your abdomen is soft and not tender. This is looking like pure gastroparesis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2198-02-10 10:03:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad it’s not something new."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2198-02-11 08:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve done really well. You’ve been tolerating oral meds and a soft diet for over 24 hours. We’re thinking you could go home tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2198-02-11 08:46:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great! What do I need to do when I get home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2198-02-11 08:47:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Continue the BRAT diet and advance slowly. Keep taking your Reglan with meals, Protonix twice daily, and your insulin as directed. We’re adding a new medication—prochlorperazine—for breakthrough nausea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2198-02-11 08:48:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that like Compazine? I’ve used that before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2198-02-11 08:49:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, same medication. You can take one tablet every six hours as needed. Also, keep using Zofran if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2198-02-11 08:50:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my blood pressure and sodium?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2198-02-11 08:51:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your BP is stable on lisinopril. For sodium, it’s still a bit low—131—but you’re not having symptoms. Follow up with your PCP in a few weeks to check it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2198-02-11 08:52:50",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. Should I worry if I start vomiting again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2198-02-11 08:53:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If you can’t keep fluids down for more than 12 hours, or if you feel weak or dizzy, come back. Otherwise, keep using your anti-nausea meds and stay in touch with your GI doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2198-02-11 08:54:50",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I have an appointment with Dr. ___ this week to check the gastric pacer."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2198-02-11 08:55:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Also, your heart murmur and mild LVH—we don’t think it’s related to this admission, but please follow up with your PCP about cardiology if you haven’t already."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2198-02-12 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All set for discharge. You’re doing well—eating, keeping meds down, and walking around. Here’s your prescription list and instructions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2198-02-12 10:16:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you so much. I’m really glad to be going home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2198-02-12 10:17:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take it slow, follow the diet, and don’t hesitate to call your doctors if you have concerns. We’ll see you in follow-up soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2198-02-12 10:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again, Dr. Lee."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2198-02-12 10:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. Have a safe trip home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2198-02-12 10:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2198-02-12 10:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will bring your discharge papers and prescriptions shortly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2198-02-12 10:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2198-02-12 10:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last thing—keep monitoring your blood sugar closely, especially as you start eating more normally."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2198-02-12 10:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I’ve been doing fingersticks every four hours like always."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2198-02-12 10:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. Once you’re back on your regular diet, resume your usual insulin sliding scale."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2198-02-12 10:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. I’ll write that down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2198-02-12 10:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. We’re all set."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2198-02-12 10:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you again for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2198-02-12 10:29:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re very welcome. Take care and feel better soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2198-02-12 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2198-02-12 10:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Have a good day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2198-02-12 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "You too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2198-02-12 10:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will be in shortly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2198-02-12 10:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thanks."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2198-02-08 11:34:00",
    "admission_end": "2198-02-12 15:30:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 30-year-old woman with Type 1 diabetes and a history of gastroparesis s/p gastric pacer presented with recurrent nausea and vomiting, just days after a prior discharge for similar symptoms. She had been tolerating oral intake until the morning of admission when she developed bilious, nonbloody vomiting. She was managed with NPO status, IV fluids, and IV antiemetics including ondansetron, prochlorperazine, and ativan. Her blood pressure, elevated on presentation, was controlled with IV metoprolol and transitioned back to oral lisinopril. Laboratory evaluation showed transient leukocytosis that resolved, mild hyponatremia (Na 130-132) likely due to vomiting and inappropriate ADH, and stable renal function. Blood and urine cultures showed no true infection. She gradually improved over 36 hours, advancing to a BRAT diet and oral medications. By discharge, she was tolerating oral intake, ambulating independently, and had stable vital signs. She was discharged home with continued antiemetics, insulin management guidance, and follow-up appointments with gastroenterology for pacer evaluation and her PCP for hypertension, hyponatremia, and cardiology referral.",
    "problems": [
      "Diabetes with neurological manifestations, type I [juvenile type], not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Hyposmolality and/or hyponatremia",
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Polyneuropathy in diabetes",
      "Aortic valve disorders",
      "Other esophagitis",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Esophageal reflux"
    ]
  }
}
